bcmdhd (101.10.591.52.27-10) stable; urgency=medium

  [ defcom5-rockchip ]
  * wl_cfg80211: handle NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3 in wl_set_wpa_version(). wpa_supplicant
    2.11 (Ubuntu 25.10/26.04, Fedora 40+) signals WPA3-Personal with VERSION_3 alone,
    where 2.10 sent VERSION_2; the driver fell through to WPA_AUTH_DISABLED, so the
    firmware tried an open association carrying an SAE RSN IE and every WPA3 or
    WPA2/WPA3 AP refused it (deauth reason 13). Same fix as the in-kernel copy
    (armbian/linux-rockchip#561), mirroring brcmfmac's brcmf_set_wpa_version().

  [ EvilOlaf ]
  * fix build on Linux 7.3: remain_on_channel and mgmt_tx get the cookie
    as u64 by value, assigned by cfg80211. Keep that cookie as the ROC id
    and TX status id, so cancel, expiry and TX status still match.

 -- Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 08:26:04 +0200

bcmdhd (101.10.591.52.27-9) stable; urgency=medium

  [ Alexey Belyaev ]
  * fix build on kernels that backported the cfg80211_port_authorized
    td_bitmap arguments: the 5-argument call was gated at 6.2.0, so a 6.1.x
    kernel carrying the change took the old 3-argument branch and failed with
    "too few arguments to function 'cfg80211_port_authorized'"

 -- Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:25:37 +0200

